-----------**------------
     prefix sum
----------**-------------
Case 1: Normal Prefix Sum (includes current element)

prefix[i] = sum of elements from 0 to i
------------------------------------------
prefix[0] = nums[0];
for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
    prefix[i] = prefix[i - 1] + nums[i];
}------------------------------------------------
Notice we use nums[i] because we want to include the current element.

Case 2: Prefix Product for "Product Except Self" (excludes current element)
prefix[i] = product of elements before i
prefix[0] = 1;
----------------------------------------------
for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
    prefix[i] = prefix[i - 1] * nums[i - 1];
}
------------------------------------------------------
Notice we use nums[i-1] because we want to exclude the current element.

---------------
Compare Both
----------------
Normal Prefix Sum
prefix[i] = prefix[i-1] + nums[i]
                     ↑
             Include current
Product Except Self Prefix
prefix[i] = prefix[i-1] * nums[i-1]
                     ↑
             Exclude current


--------**-------------
       Suffix
----------**-----------
What is a Suffix?
A suffix means everything to the right.
Normal Suffix Sum (Includes Current Element)
suffix[i] = sum from i to n-1

------------------------------------
suffix[n-1] = nums[n-1];

for(int i=n-2; i>=0; i--){
    suffix[i] = suffix[i+1] + nums[i];
}
--------------------------------------


Suffix for Product Except Self (Excludes Current Element)
suffix[i] = product of elements AFTER i
suffix[i] = product of elements AFTER i

suffix[i] = suffix[i+1] * nums[i+1];

------------------------------------------------------
Prefix = everything left of the wall → use i - 1
Suffix = everything right of the wall → use i + 1

// Product before current
prefix[i] = prefix[i-1] * nums[i-1];

// Product after current
suffix[i] = suffix[i+1] * nums[i+1];
--------------------------------------------------------

Example 1:

Input: nums = [1,2,4,6]

Output: [48,24,12,8]


class Solution {
    public int[] productExceptSelf(int[] nums) {
        int n=nums.length;
      int ans[] = new int[n];
      int prefix[] = new int[n];
      int suffix[] = new int[n];

      prefix[0]=1;
      suffix[n-1]=1;

      for(int i=1;i<n;i++)
      {
        prefix[i]=prefix[i-1]*nums[i-1];
      }
       for(int i=n-2;i>=0;i--)
      {
        suffix[i]=suffix[i+1]*nums[i+1];
      }
       for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
      {
        ans[i]=prefix[i]*suffix[i];
      }

      return ans;

        
    }
}  




             
